  {
    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "For the first time, the personalities and approaches of the leading models are diverging in significant ways, magnified by the fact that over longer task horizons these differences in judgement &amp; approach are magnified. You really need to test the models for yourself/your firm.",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
    "url": "https://twitter.com/emollick/status/2075596439485386829",
    "time": "2026-07-10 23:02",
    "created_at": "Fri Jul 10 15:02:08 +0000 2026",
    "id_str": "2075596439485386829",
    "is_retweet": false
  },
  {
    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "You can no longer just drop in the smartest model into a harness and expect it to behave similarly to any other model of similar ability levels. This is starting to look a lot more like hiring for a role.\n\nPublic benchmarks don't show this well, you need to figure out your tests.",
